# Correct only conversion errors where generated output differs from the…

Correct only conversion errors where generated output differs from the
original source evidence.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] Correct only conversion errors where generated output differs from the
  original source evidence.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

World material publication no longer applies the historical identity-specific
Lard Lad RGB-complement recipe. P3D texture extraction already copies embedded
image payload bytes directly, and no tracked source or conversion evidence
authorized rewriting one shader/file-name pair after extraction. Recovered PNG
bytes are now content-addressed and published unchanged. A typed regression
requires the prepared texture payload to equal the source bytes and derives its
SHA-256/file identity from those same bytes. Strict pipeline Clippy is clean.

This umbrella task remains open for other reported conversion differences that
need direct source-backed evidence before any correction is admitted.
